Philip Potter <p...@doc.ic.ac.uk> wrote:
>
> I admit there is /some/ precedent for this in RPG systems. I seem to
> recall that in MERP (Middle-Earth Role Playing) there were two types of
> magic - "essence" and "channelling" which were "wizardly" and "priestly"
> magic - and that one was more lenient on armour than the other.

In Nethack strange stuff happens when spells are cast or
wands are zapped.  I think that maps into the "essence"
concept - Stuff any being can do because it's a part of
how that world works, but that is limited by skill restrictions.
So grid bugs are restricted in almost everything while
player characters have much wider ranges.

In Nethack strange stuff happens when you pray and/or
when you drop stuff on altars.  I think this maps into the
"channelling" concept - Stuff that certain beings can do, but
that is limited by species.  So dragons can lay eggs, monsters
with arms can wield weapons, dieties can manifest artifacts.
Since Surt from the Valk quest is in lore a diety, he should be
able to manifest an artifact weapon or create an altar.


